Subject: [PATCH] mail: Add applied.sh to find patches trunk applied
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: vmtxrlwvnlnwstpzskqwytqmwvskmonl

Pat applies patches from the list without replying to each one, so
nothing on the list says which patches landed, and the review queue
cannot be cleared without checking trunk by hand.

The change id cannot make the link, because git am drops it and the
applied commit gets a new one.  The diff survives, though: git
patch-id --stable gives a patch and the commit it became the same id
even after git am, a rebase, or a reworded message.  Matching on it
needs nothing extra in Pat's commits, and the answer is the same on
every run.

A patch edited before it was applied gets a new id and is not found;
those still need a person, or a reviewer, to say so.
